  "details": "See: https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/class-LightProbeProxyVolume.html\nWithout, mesh renderers can only be influenced by one tetrahedron of light probes. Because it is only one sample point, it will look weird when crossing from dark to bright light probes. E.g. when standing in a dark area and stretching out your arm in front of a bright light probe does not light only arm.\nIt shouldn't be that performance intensive, but a limit on the maximum amount of probes in light probe proxy volumes would probably be useful.",
